.TH RASPIBACKUP 1 "@DATE@" "raspiBackup @VERSION@" "raspiBackup Manual"
.SH NAME
raspiBackup \- create and restore backups of a running Raspberry Pi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raspiBackup
.RI [ option ]...
.RI [ backupPath ]
.br
.B raspiBackup
.B \-d
.I restoreDevice
.RI [ option ]...
.I backup
.br
.B raspiBackup
.BR \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B raspiBackup
creates full backups of a running Raspberry Pi system and restores them
to an SD card, USB disk, NVMe or any other block device.
Backups are created with
.BR dd (1),
.BR tar (1)
or
.BR rsync (1).
rsync backups use hardlinks to the previous backup, so only new and
changed files consume additional space.
.PP
Each backup is stored in a directory
.IR backupPath / hostname / hostname \- type \-backup\- YYYYmmdd\-HHMMSS
on the backup path.
A configurable number of backups is kept; older ones are deleted
automatically (see
.B \-k
and
.BR \-\-smartRecycle ).
.PP
In
.I normal mode
the boot and root partition are saved.
In
.I partition oriented mode
.RB ( \-P ,
.BR \-T )
any number of partitions can be saved and restored individually.
.PP
Services which modify data on disk (databases, web servers and the like)
should be stopped during the backup; see
.B \-o
and
.BR \-a .
.PP
.B raspiBackup
has to be run as root.
Defaults for all options are read from the configuration files described in
.BR raspiBackup.conf (5).
Command line options override the configuration.
.PP
Boolean options can be suffixed with
.B +
to enable or
.B \-
to disable them, e.g.
.B \-z\-
disables compression even when it is enabled in the configuration.
Without suffix the option is enabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General options
.TP
.BI \-b " blocksize"
Block size used by
.BR dd .
Default: 1M.
.TP
.BI \-D " parameters"
Additional parameters passed to
.BR dd .
.TP
.BI \-e " address"
eMail address to send the completion status to.
.TP
.BI \-E " parameters"
Additional parameters passed to the eMail program.
.TP
.BI \-\-eMailColoring " mode"
How warnings and errors are colored in eMails:
.B SUBJECT
or
.BR OPTION .
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Use
.I file
as additional configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-forceEmail [ +|\- ]
Always send an eMail, even if
.B DEFAULT_MAIL_ON_ERROR_ONLY
is set.
.TP
.BR \-g [ +|\- ]
Display a progress bar.
.TP
.BI \-G " language"
Message language:
.BR EN ,
.BR DE ,
.B FI
or
.BR FR .
Default: system language, falling back to English.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BI \-l " level"
Log level:
.B Off
or
.BR Debug .
Default: Debug.
.TP
.BI \-L " target"
Location of the log file:
.B Varlog
.RI ( /var/log/raspiBackup/ hostname .log ),
.B Backup
(the backup directory),
.B Current
(the current directory)
or the absolute name of a file.
Default: Backup.
.TP
.BI \-m " level"
Message level:
.B Minimal
or
.BR Detailed .
Default: Minimal.
.TP
.BI \-M " description"
Create a snapshot.
.I description
is appended to the backup directory name.
.TP
.BI \-N " extensions"
Space separated list of extensions to call before and after the backup.
See
.B EXTENSIONS
below.
.TP
.BR \-\-notifyStart [ +|\- ]
Also send a notification when the backup starts.
.TP
.BI \-s " program"
eMail program:
.BR mail ,
.BR ssmtp ,
.BR msmtp ,
.B sendEmail
or
.B mailext
(eMail extension).
Default: mail.
.TP
.BR \-\-systemstatus [ +|\- ]
Write the system status (active services, open files) into the debug log.
.TP
.BI \-\-telegramToken " token"
.TQ
.BI \-\-telegramChatID " id"
.TQ
.BI \-\-telegramThreadID " id"
.TQ
.BI \-\-telegramNotifications " flags"
Telegram notification settings.
See the corresponding
.B DEFAULT_TELEGRAM_*
options in
.BR raspiBackup.conf (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-timestamps [ +|\- "], " \-\-ts [ +|\- ]
Prefix all messages with a timestamp.
.TP
.BI \-u " excludes"
Additional excludes for tar and rsync backups.
The value has to be valid for the backup tool used, e.g.
.BR "\(dq\-\-exclude=/home/pi/.cache \-\-exclude=/var/tmp\(dq" .
.TP
.BR \-\-unsupportedEnvironment ", " \-\-use
Run in an environment which is not supported (not a Raspberry Pi or
an operating system other than Raspberry Pi OS).
Use at your own risk.
.TP
.BR \-\-updateConfig [ +|\- ]
Merge new options of the current release into the existing configuration
file
.IR /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf .
The old configuration is saved as
.IR raspiBackup.conf.bak .
.TP
.BR \-v [ +|\- ]
Verbose output of the backup tools.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version, commit and commit date and exit.
.TP
.B \-Y
Answer all questions with yes.
Use with care!
.SS Backup options
.TP
.BI \-a " commands"
Commands to start services after the backup, separated by
.BR && .
Use
.B \(dq:\(dq
if no service has to be started.
.TP
.BR \-B [ +|\- ]
Save the boot partition with
.B tar
instead of
.BR dd .
.TP
.BI \-\-bootDevice " device"
Device of the boot partition, if it cannot be detected automatically.
.TP
.BR \-c [ +|\- ]
Skip the check whether the backup path is a mounted remote or external
partition.
.TP
.BI \-\-clone " device"
Clone the running system onto
.I device
after the backup.
.TP
.BR \-F [ +|\- ]
Simulate the backup.
No backup is created.
.TP
.BI \-\-dynamicMount " partition"
Mount
.I partition
(a device or a mountpoint defined in
.IR /etc/fstab )
before the backup and unmount it afterwards.
.TP
.BR \-\-ignoreAdditionalPartitions [ +|\- ]
In normal mode, ignore partitions with a number greater than 2.
.TP
.B \-\-ignoreMissingPartitions
Allow to back up fewer partitions than were saved in the previous
partition oriented backup.
.TP
.BI \-k " number"
Number of backups to keep.
Ignored if smart recycle is enabled.
Default: 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep_dd " number"
.TQ
.BI \-\-keep_ddz " number"
.TQ
.BI \-\-keep_tar " number"
.TQ
.BI \-\-keep_tgz " number"
.TQ
.BI \-\-keep_rsync " number"
Number of backups to keep for a specific backup type.
0 means the value of
.B \-k
is used.
.TP
.BI \-o " commands"
Commands to stop services before the backup, separated by
.BR && .
Use
.B \(dq:\(dq
if no service has to be stopped.
.TP
.BI \-p " path"
Backup path.
Overrides the positional
.I backupPath
argument and
.BR DEFAULT_BACKUPPATH .
.TP
.BR \-P [ +|\- ]
Use partition oriented mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-rebootSystem [ +|\- ]
Reboot the system when the backup has finished.
.TP
.BR \-\-smartRecycle [ +|\- ]
Use the smart recycle strategy to decide which backups are kept.
.TP
.BR \-\-smartRecycleDryrun [ +|\- ]
Only report which backups smart recycle would delete.
Enabled by default; disable it with
.B \-\-smartRecycleDryrun\-
to actually delete backups.
.TP
.BI \-\-smartRecycleOptions " \(dqd w m y\(dq"
Number of daily, weekly, monthly and yearly backups to keep with smart
recycle.
Default: \(dq7 4 12 1\(dq.
.TP
.BI \-t " type"
Backup type:
.BR dd ,
.B tar
or
.BR rsync .
Default: rsync.
.TP
.BI \-T " partitions"
Partitions to back up in partition oriented mode, e.g.
.B \(dq1 2 5\(dq
or
.B \(dq*\(dq
for all partitions.
Implies
.BR \-P .
.TP
.BR \-\-tarCompressionTool ", " \-\-tct " \fItool\fR"
Compress tar backups with
.I tool
instead of gzip:
.BR bzip2 ,
.BR gzip ,
.BR lzip ,
.BR lzma ,
.BR lzop ,
.BR xz ,
.B zstd
or
.BR lz4 .
Ignored if
.B \-z
is used.
.TP
.BR \-\-tarCompressionToolOptions ", " \-\-tcto " \fIoptions\fR"
Options passed to the tar compression tool.
.TP
.BR \-x [ +|\- ]
Don't save the boot partition with
.B dd
in rsync and tar backups.
.TP
.BR \-z [ +|\- ]
Compress dd and tar backups.
.SS Restore options
.TP
.BI \-d " device"
Restore the backup onto
.IR device ,
e.g.
.IR /dev/sda .
All data on
.I device
will be lost.
.TP
.BR \-0 [ +|\- ]
Don't partition the restore device.
The existing partitions are used.
.TP
.BR \-00 [ +|\- ]
Don't partition and don't format the restore device (rsync backups only).
.TP
.BR \-1 [ +|\- ]
Ignore formatting errors on the restore device.
.TP
.BR \-C [ +|\- ]
Check for bad blocks when formatting the restore device.
This takes a long time.
.TP
.BI \-R " partition"
Restore the root partition onto
.I partition
(e.g.
.IR /dev/sdb1 )
and the boot partition onto
.BR \-d .
.TP
.BR \-\-resizeRootFS [ +|\- "], " \-\-resizeLastPartitionFS [ +|\- ]
Resize the root filesystem (or the last partition in partition oriented
mode) to the size of the restore device.
Enabled by default.
.TP
.BI \-T " partitions"
Partitions to restore from a partition oriented backup, e.g.
.B \(dq1 2\(dq
or
.B \(dq*\(dq
for all partitions.
.TP
.BR \-\-updateUUIDs [ +|\- ]
Assign new UUIDs and PARTUUIDs to the restored partitions, so the
restored device can be used in parallel to the original one.
Enabled by default.
.SH EXTENSIONS
Extensions are bash scripts which are called at specific points of a backup
or restore.
An extension named
.I name
consists of the files
.RI /usr/local/bin/raspiBackup_ name _pre.sh
and
.RI /usr/local/bin/raspiBackup_ name _post.sh .
They are enabled with
.B \-N
or
.B DEFAULT_EXTENSIONS
(backup) and
.B DEFAULT_RESTORE_EXTENSIONS
(restore).
.PP
Sample extensions which report memory usage, CPU temperature and disk
usage are shipped in
.I /usr/local/share/raspibackup/extensions
and can be enabled with
.BR raspiBackupInstallUI (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf
System wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.raspiBackup.conf
Configuration of the calling user.
.TP
.I ./.raspiBackup.conf
Configuration in the current directory.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/raspibackup/raspiBackup_{en,de}.conf
Configuration templates.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/systemd/system/raspiBackup.{service,timer}
systemd units to run regular backups.
.TP
.IR /var/log/raspiBackup/ hostname .log
Log file if the log target is
.BR Varlog .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 101\-148
An error occurred.
The message issued before termination explains the cause, for example
107 (invalid parameter), 108 (missing files), 116 (restore failed),
120 (missing commands) or 131 (mount failed).
.SH EXAMPLES
Create an rsync backup on
.I /backup
and keep the last 5 backups:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo raspiBackup \-t rsync \-k 5 /backup
.RE
.PP
Create a backup and stop and start services around it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B sudo raspiBackup \-o \(dqsystemctl stop nginx && systemctl stop mariadb\(dq \e
.B \ \ \ \ \-a \(dqsystemctl start mariadb && systemctl start nginx\(dq
.fi
.RE
.PP
Restore a backup to
.IR /dev/sda :
.PP
.RS
.B sudo raspiBackup \-d /dev/sda /backup/raspberrypi/raspberrypi\-rsync\-backup\-20261030\-120000
.RE
.PP
Create a snapshot before an upgrade:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo raspiBackup \-M \(dqbefore upgrade\(dq
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR raspiBackup.conf (5),
.BR raspiBackupInstallUI (1),
.BR dd (1),
.BR tar (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
.UR https://raspibackup.linux-tips-and-tricks.de/en/home/
